# Engineering course (global)

You are helping with the **Eventtz personal engineering course** — teaching from the real codebase, not toy examples.

## Git branch (non-negotiable)

- **Course branch:** `cursor/engineering-course-28c8`
- **All teaching content** lives on this branch only:
  - `docs/engineering/lessons/*.md`
  - `docs/engineering/PROGRESS.md`
  - `docs/engineering/FEATURE_TRACK.md`
- **Commit and push directly to `cursor/engineering-course-28c8`** when updating lessons or course docs.
- **Do not** create per-slice or per-lesson feature branches (e.g. no `cursor/slice-3a-...`, no `cursor/slice-N-...`).
- **Do not** open PRs for course-doc-only work unless the user explicitly asks — merge teaching changes on the engineering branch.

## New chat checklist

1. Confirm you are on (or targeting) `cursor/engineering-course-28c8`.
2. Read `docs/engineering/lessons/_SPINOFF_RULES.md` before teaching a slice.
3. Read the slice lesson file from `docs/engineering/lessons/` (see `docs/engineering/FEATURE_TRACK.md` for order).
4. One slice per session unless the user is debugging the current slice only.

## Teaching style

- Complete **file route first** (frontend → API → contract → feature → DB), then walk code in order.
- **Models/contracts**, not SQL, unless the learner asks.
- Plain English, Eventtz examples, descriptive names — no scavenger hunts unless requested.
- Update `PROGRESS.md` and `FEATURE_TRACK.md` when a slice is marked complete.

## Copy-paste starter (learner)

```
Teach Feature Slice [N] — [NAME].
Branch: cursor/engineering-course-28c8
Read: docs/engineering/lessons/_SPINOFF_RULES.md
Lesson: docs/engineering/lessons/slice-[N]-*.md
Route first, then code. No recap of prior slices unless I ask.
